Z||000000||fierospeeder||09-08-2000||08:25 AM||||I was just watching hotrod tv and i seen it before but missed the intro, but it was stating that illinois, state im from, and florida is having some sort of legislation that is deciding that the cars in junkyards should be scrapped.  I tried going to the link but its gone, that they gave but its gone.<P>In californa, they are trying to do the same thing.<P>check out this site <A HREF="http://www.sema.org/fedleg/stateredhot/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.sema.org/fedleg/stateredhot/</A> <P>also this site has a link to that site plus other great car info<BR> <A HREF="http://www.enjoythedrive.com" TARGET=_blank>www.enjoythedrive.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||09-08-2000||02:16 PM||||The EPA has been on junk yards for years. The yards have litterally been given a decade or more to make them selves cleaner and most operator have chosen not to do so. Many won't even do basic things like drain fluids.<P>CARB has a problem, but then when don't they. There scrapage rules are likely headed to very high state and maybe federal court.<P>There are scrapage laws of some kind in a large number of states.  Most of the regs I've seen so far require crushing the cars. It's not something new.<P>Even if the law didn't require crushing there's only so much yard space available to put them. I see allot of Fieros here in DE head straight for the crusher as soon as the yard gets them. Why? the yard operators are out of space and won't keep cars they don't think will make money for them. I'd buy more stuff off them but there's only so much money and space I have.<P>As sorry as I am, you just can't save everything.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 09-08-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||rockcrawl||09-08-2000||10:40 PM||||Here in PA they are required to remove the catalyst; result, destroyed an otherwise perfect dual outlet exhaust system. <P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||13
